DankMaterialShell on Arch (active shell)
========================================

Saved 2026-10-24. On this date the Arch install moved its desktop shell from
caelestia-shell-mango to DankMaterialShell (DMS). The compositor did not
change: still MangoWC. This folder is the current, active setup. Everything
under ../config/mangoconfigs/ (caelestia/, mangowc/) is the previous
Caelestia-era setup, kept for reference and rollback only.

Like the rest of rice/, this is a plain COPY of the live files. Nothing here is
managed or symlinked by Home Manager; editing a file here changes nothing on
the running system.

Stack
-----

Compositor   mangowm-git 0.15.5, held back on purpose (IgnorePkg = mangowm-git
             in /etc/pacman.conf). Its config still uses the old key names
             (borderpx, gappih, bordercolor, ...) which mango 0.18+ ignores,
             so do not upgrade it without migrating conf.d/ first.
Shell        DMS 2.0.0, the official tagged release, installed user-local in
             ~/.local/opt/dms-2.0.0 (no pacman package yet). bin/dms is a
             one-line wrapper that makes `dms` resolve to it.
Fallback     the pacman package dms-shell 1.6.3 is still installed underneath
             (/usr/bin/dms); `rm ~/.local/bin/dms` brings it back.
Quickshell   quickshell-git 0.3.2
Fonts        Google Sans Flex (UI), JetBrainsMono Nerd Font (mono)

Layout
------

config/settings.json   -> ~/.config/dms/settings.json. Starts from the DMS 2.0
                          settings of the Void install (see ../../void-linux),
                          then local choices: fonts, popup/dock transparency
                          0.7, frame mode "separate" (launcher opens
                          centered). ~/.config/DankMaterialShell is now a
                          symlink to ~/.config/dms (DMS 2.0 migrated it).
mango/                 -> ~/.config/mango. config.conf sources conf.d/*.conf
                          and two DMS-generated files from mango/dms/ (colors
                          and windowrules). dms/layout.conf is deliberately NOT
                          sourced so the gaps/borders in conf.d/ stay in
                          charge. idle.sh is the swayidle script.
bin/dms                -> ~/.local/bin/dms (wrapper, see above)
bin/super-tap          -> ~/.local/bin/super-tap. Tapping Super alone opens the
                          launcher; Super+<key> combos are ignored. It watches
                          /dev/input passively (needs the `input` group) and is
                          started from mango/conf.d/autostart.conf.
wallpaper/lock-screen.png  the lock screen background (settings.json has
                          lockScreenWallpaperPath pointing at
                          ~/Pictures/toji-zenin/<name>.png)

Keybinds (Caelestia command -> DMS)
-----------------------------------

Same keys as before, only the command behind them changed:

SUPER+d            launcher        dms ipc call spotlight toggle
SUPER+a            dashboard       dms ipc call dash toggle ""
SUPER+SHIFT+m      dashboard       dms ipc call dash toggle ""
SUPER+, / SUPER+w  control center  dms ipc call control-center toggle
SUPER+i            notifications   dms ipc call notifications toggle
SUPER+SHIFT+i      clear notifs    dms ipc call notifications clearAll
SUPER+x            lock            dms ipc call lock lock
SUPER+SHIFT+e      power menu      dms ipc call powermenu toggle
SUPER+CTRL+w       wallpaper       random file from ~/Pictures/wallpapers via
                                   dms ipc call wallpaper set
SUPER+v            clipboard       dms ipc call clipboard toggle
SUPER+ALT+n        notepad         dms ipc call notepad toggle
SUPER+ALT+s        DMS settings    dms ipc call settings focusOrToggle
SUPER+SHIFT+w      DMS settings    ... focusOrToggleWith personalization
volume/mute/mic    XF86 keys and SUPER+SHIFT+F1..F3,F10 -> dms ipc call audio
brightness         XF86 keys and SUPER+SHIFT+F7/F8 -> dms ipc call brightness
                   increment|decrement 5 ""

Quirks worth remembering: `dash toggle` and `brightness ...` need an explicit
(empty) trailing argument or the IPC call fails with "Too few arguments".
SUPER+ALT+s used to cycle the scroller proportion preset; that bind is kept
commented out in binds.conf.

Other changes made during the move
----------------------------------

- swayosd-server is no longer started; DMS draws its own volume/brightness OSD.
- idle.sh locks with `dms ipc call lock lock`. It used to write to
  ~/.cache/qs/lock, a trigger only the old kamalen shell watched, so idle and
  pre-suspend locking silently did nothing for a while.
- Layer animations are off (layer_animations=0 in conf.d/animations.conf): with
  them on, every DMS panel slid in from an edge.
- A window rule makes the DMS 2.0 Settings window float (app id
  dev.duxlabs.shell; 1.6.3 used com.danklinux.dms).
- The notification daemon is DMS now. Only one shell may run at a time.

Known caveats
-------------

- Background blur: mango does not implement ext-background-effect-v1, so DMS
  reports "Unsupported". Blur still happens, but through mango's own
  blur_layer on DMS layer surfaces.
- Upstream DMS master switched its generated mango files to snake_case key
  names (border_color, ...) for mango 0.18+. Mango 0.15.5 only knows the old
  ones (bordercolor, ...). The v2.0.0 build used here still wrote the old
  names (see mango/dms/colors.conf), but a newer DMS may not; if the border
  colours stop following the wallpaper, this is why, and the static colours
  in conf.d/colors.conf apply instead.
- A newer DMS (2.x) will be packaged in Arch as dux-shell. When it lands,
  remove ~/.local/bin/dms and install the package, after checking it still
  works with mango 0.15.5.

Restore
-------

1. Install quickshell-git, matugen, accountsservice and the optional deps DMS
   lists (cava, i2c-tools, qt6ct, qt6-multimedia, wtype, kimageformats, ...).
2. Download dms-full-amd64.tar.gz from the DMS v2.0.0 release, verify its
   .sha256, and unpack it to ~/.local/opt/dms-2.0.0. (Or install the dms-shell
   package for 1.6.3; settings.json is 2.0 format, so some keys are ignored.)
3. cp bin/* ~/.local/bin/ and chmod +x them.
4. cp config/settings.json ~/.config/dms/ and
   cp -a mango/. ~/.config/mango/
5. Put lock-screen.png at the path named in settings.json.
6. Reload mango (SUPER+CTRL+r) and start the shell with `dms run`.
